			<div class="content" id="post-content-1308433">
									

<p>&quot;affected trains&quot;, not &quot;effected trains&quot;. And I like the idea, although personally I'd prefer if the passengers weren't affected in the second scenario other than the usual panic over &quot;our train's not stopping and I think we're picking up speed!&quot;</p>
<p>And honestly, I'm a little bit skeptical about that second scenario not happening often. Most trains I've been around, it's pretty visible whether there's a driver and most train stations have a mirror along the tracks for the driver to use to do a quick spot check as he's leaving the station. Maybe restrict it to people trying to interact with the driver by opening the door/curtain and attempts to interfere with the train?</p>

