														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1308437">
									

<p>The reason I like the craziness in this one is that it is believable though. It's not &quot;everyone on board goes crazy (TO DEAAATH)&quot; but it is &quot;everyone on board is under stress and reacts in different ways, we've noticed that some of these reactions are beyond what would be expected of natural causes&quot;</p>
<p>That makes it feels like a more genuine haunting or fear effect beyond some cheezy thing where everyone always over reacts in the same terrible way. Things that make people lose control should always be random and inconsistent because people are different.</p>
<p>And imagine the setting&#8230; you're riding a train and it starts getting too fast, you panic and look around and everyone else is a little scared&#8230; and then it gets surreal, some people are holding their heads in pain and the nice old lady across the way starts tearing at her face and THEN and some big burly dudes are throwing gas grenades and trying to restrain her. That's a scene from a horror movie.</p>

							</div>

								
					
